error[E0277]: `Cons<Id, Cons<Flag, notko_hlist::Empty>>` has no place for `Other`
  --> tests/ui/a_call_of_with_on_a_field_not_listed_is_refused.rs:36:18
   |
36 |     let _ = word.with(Other, Bool::TRUE);
   |                  ^^^^ the trait `PlaceOf<Other, There<There<_>>>` is not implemented for `Cons<Id, Cons<Flag, notko_hlist::Empty>>`
   |
   = note: A member is at `Here` when it is the head of a `Cons`, and at `There<P>` when the tail holds it at `P`. The usual cause is a member the list does not hold. If the compiler reports `type annotations needed` instead, the list holds the member at more than one place. If it reports `overflow evaluating the requirement`, the walk is one step per cell and the list is deeper than the default recursion limit, so the crate root wants `#![recursion_limit = "1024"]`.
note: required by a bound in `Word::<L>::with`
  --> src/word.rs
   |
   |     pub const fn with<F: Field, P: Place>(self, _field: F, to: F::Value) -> Self
   |                  ---- required by a bound in this associated function
   |     where
   |         L::Fields: PlaceOf<F, P> + Below<P>,
   |                    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ required by this bound in `Word::<L>::with`

